Patch 2502: shadow maps rendered at SHADOW_SCALE times the guest size (1-4, default 2; 1 = the game's own size).

Depth surfaces the title samples through a depth comparison are flagged as shadow maps; their depth-only passes size
them at the scale and the replay viewport scales the guest rect. Receivers sample with normalised coordinates and the
comparison helper takes the size from the bound texture, so only the surface, its colour copy and the passes'
viewports change. At J-Stars' own 2048x1024 the shadow texels are large next to thin parts (sleeves, shoulder plates)
and showed as grey stair-step lines moving with the camera; RPCS3 at a 300% resolution scale draws them at 3x. The
launcher's Shadows option (Low/Medium/High/Ultra = 1/2/3/4).

Tested (US disc, quick Free Battle route): SHADOW_SCALE=2 29.94 flips/s (bench/exp/2026-11-09_0246-shscale2),
SHADOW_SCALE=3 29.75 (bench/feature/2026-11-09_1604-shadow3); intros and fight look right.

